  "pse": {
    "problem": "Determining which data from multiple parties should participate in federated learning for improving the accuracy of model training.",
    "solution_function": "The system coordinates client terminals to extract sample data according to common rules for participation in horizontal federated learning, improving the quality and representativeness of the training dataset.",
    "solution_structure": "Client terminals, each with local sample data sets and a processing unit (possibly software) to interpret instructions and apply sample extraction rules.",
    "solution_implementation": "Client terminals receive data processing instructions containing sample extraction rules. The instructions are used to determine the sample data value ranges for extraction based on target features. For each range, the system selects relevant samples from the local dataset and combines them as multiple pieces of target sample data.",
    "effect": "Improved model training accuracy due to more diverse and representative data participation in federated learning"
  },
